{"abstract":[{"text":"People enjoy the vibrant content, immersive experiences, and streamlined interactions that tvOS delivers in media and games, as well as in fitness, education, and home utility apps.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/technologies","doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/human-interface-guidelines","doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/getting-started"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/designing-for-tvos"},"kind":"article","legalNotices":{"copyright":"Copyright &copy; 2026 Apple Inc. All rights reserved.","privacyPolicy":"https:\/\/www.apple.com\/privacy\/privacy-policy","termsOfUse":"https:\/\/www.apple.com\/legal\/internet-services\/terms\/site.html"},"metadata":{"availableLanguages":["en-US","zh-CN","ja-JP","ko-KR"],"images":[{"identifier":"tvos.svg","type":"icon"},{"identifier":"platforms-designing-for-tvos-thumbnail.png","type":"card"}],"role":"article","title":"Designing for tvOS"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"platforms-tvOS-intro.png","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"As you begin designing your app or game for tvOS, start by understanding the following fundamental device characteristics and patterns that distinguish the tvOS experience. Using these characteristics and patterns to inform your design decisions can help you provide an app or game that tvOS users appreciate.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Display.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A TV typically has a very large, high-resolution display.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ergonomics.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Although people generally remain many feet away from their stationary TV — often 8 feet or more — they sometimes continue to interact with content as they move around the room.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Inputs.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" People can use a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/remotes","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/game-controls","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", their ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/siri","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and apps running on their other devices to interact with Apple TV.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"App interactions.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" People can get deeply immersed in a single experience — often lasting hours — but they also appreciate using a picture-in-picture view to simultaneously follow an alternative app or video.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"System features.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Apple TV users expect their apps and games to integrate well with the following system experiences.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/playing-video#Integrating-with-the-TV-app","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/shareplay","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/top-shelf","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/managing-accounts#TV-provider-accounts","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Best-practices","level":2,"text":"Best practices","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Great tvOS experiences integrate the platform and device capabilities that people value most. To help your experience feel at home in tvOS, prioritize the following ways to incorporate these features and capabilities.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Support powerful, delightful interactions through the fluid, familiar gestures people make with the Siri Remote.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Embrace the tvOS focus system, letting it gently highlight and expand onscreen items as people move among them, helping them know what to do and where they are at all times.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Deliver beautiful, edge-to-edge artwork, subtle and fluid animations, and engaging audio, wrapping people in a rich, cinematic experience that’s clear, legible, and captivating from across the room.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Enhance multiuser support by making sign-in easy and infrequent, handling shared sign-in, and automatically switching profiles when people change the current viewer.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Resources","level":2,"text":"Resources","type":"heading"},{"anchor":"Related","level":4,"text":"Related","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/resources\/#tvos-apps","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Developer-documentation","level":4,"text":"Developer documentation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/tvos\/get-started\/","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Videos","level":4,"text":"Videos","type":"heading"},{"items":["doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/videos\/play\/wwdc2020\/10042"],"style":"compactGrid","type":"links"},{"anchor":"Change-log","level":2,"text":"Change log","type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Date","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Changes","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"September 14, 2022","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Refined best practices for multiuser support.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"topicSectionsStyle":"compactGrid","references":{"B17CF999-313D-4C0D-A791-D2A5DD5F9242":{"alt":null,"identifier":"B17CF999-313D-4C0D-A791-D2A5DD5F9242","type":"image","variants":[{"traits":["1x"],"url":"https:\/\/devimages-cdn.apple.com\/wwdc-services\/images\/49\/B17CF999-313D-4C0D-A791-D2A5DD5F9242\/3789_wide_250x141_1x.jpg"},{"traits":["2x"],"url":"https:\/\/devimages-cdn.apple.com\/wwdc-services\/images\/49\/B17CF999-313D-4C0D-A791-D2A5DD5F9242\/3789_wide_250x141_2x.jpg"},{"traits":["3x"],"url":"https:\/\/devimages-cdn.apple.com\/wwdc-services\/images\/49\/B17CF999-313D-4C0D-A791-D2A5DD5F9242\/3789_wide_250x141_3x.jpg"}]},"components-top-shelf-thumbnail.png":{"alt":"A stylized representation of a horizontal list of media previews above a row of Apple TV apps. The image is tinted red to subtly reflect the red in the original six-color Apple logo.","identifier":"components-top-shelf-thumbnail.png","type":"image","variants":[{"traits":["2x","light"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.HIG\/components-top-shelf-thumbnail@2x.png"},{"traits":["2x","dark"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.HIG\/components-top-shelf-thumbnail~dark@2x.png"}]},"doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/getting-started":{"abstract":[{"text":"Create an app or game that feels at home on every platform you support.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/getting-started","images":[{"identifier":"overview.svg","type":"icon"},{"identifier":"platforms.png","type":"card"}],"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Getting started","type":"topic","url":"\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/getting-started"},"doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/managing-accounts#TV-provider-accounts":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/managing-accounts#TV-provider-accounts","kind":"section","title":"TV provider accounts","type":"topic","url":"\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/managing-accounts#TV-provider-accounts"},"doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/playing-video#Integrating-with-the-TV-app":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/playing-video#Integrating-with-the-TV-app","kind":"section","title":"Integrating with the TV app","type":"topic","url":"\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/playing-video#Integrating-with-the-TV-app"},"doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/shareplay":{"abstract":[{"text":"SharePlay lets people experience activities together from anywhere, whether they’re watching a movie, playing a game, or sketching on a whiteboard.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/shareplay","images":[{"identifier":"shareplay.svg","type":"icon"},{"identifier":"technologies-shareplay-thumbnail.png","type":"card"}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SharePlay","type":"topic","url":"\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/shareplay"},"doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/top-shelf":{"abstract":[{"text":"The Apple TV Home Screen provides an area called Top Shelf, which showcases your content in a rich, engaging way while also giving people access to their favorite apps in the Dock.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/Human-Interface-Guidelines\/top-shelf","images":[{"identifier":"components-top-shelf-thumbnail.png","type":"card"}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Top Shelf","type":"topic","url":"\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/top-shelf"},"doc://com.apple.HIG/design/human-interface-guidelines":{"abstract":[{"text":"The HIG contains guidance and best practices that can help you design a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"great experience for any Apple platform.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.HIG\/design\/human-interface-guidelines","images":[{"identifier":"human-interface-guidelines-page-image-card.png","type":"card"}],"kind":"article","role":"collection","title":"Human Interface Guidelines","type":"topic","url":"\/design\/human-interface-guidelines"},"doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/technologies":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/technologies","kind":"technologies","role":"overview","title":"Technologies","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/technologies"},"doc://com.apple.documentation/videos/play/wwdc2020/10042":{"abstract":[{"text":"Add a new dimension to your tvOS app with SwiftUI. We’ll show you how to build layouts powered by SwiftUI and customize your interface with custom buttons, provide more functionality in your app with a context menu, check if views are focused, and manage default focus.\n\nTo get the most out of this session, you should be comfortable with SwiftUI. For a primer, watch “Introducing SwiftUI: Building Your First App” and “SwiftUI On All Devices.”","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/videos\/play\/wwdc2020\/10042","images":[{"identifier":"B17CF999-313D-4C0D-A791-D2A5DD5F9242","type":"card"}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Build SwiftUI apps for tvOS","type":"topic","url":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/videos\/play\/wwdc2020\